    "explanation": "To both parties: this case is escalated to a human reviewer and no money moves. The SGD 6.00 no-show fee is HELD — not collected from the rider and not refunded — until the missing evidence is resolved.\n\nThe charge stands or falls on POL-NS-01, which the driver must satisfy on all four limbs. Limbs (a) and (d) are met: the trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 21:10:20 and records the trip terminated by the driver at 21:15:40 under cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding. Limbs (b) and (c), however, are read by the clause from the gps_trace alone — (b) placing the driver inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius at or before the arrival event, and (c) measuring a continuous 300-second in-geofence dwell from the first qualifying fix, not from the arrival tap. The trace, EV-GPS-09109, is MISSING: no payload, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT (severity BLOCKING). Under POL-GEN-02(3) it can carry no fact, and a trace with no fixes at all is impaired under POL-NS-08(b). It is neither proof the driver was at the bay nor proof he was not.\n\nSo the rider cannot be given a refund either. The rider's claim is that the car was not at the bay; without the trace there is no qualifying in-radius reading to fail limb (b), and the policy is explicit that a trace too sparse to establish in-radius readings is impaired rather than proof of absence (POL-NS-02). Limb (b) is therefore undecided and supports neither the fee nor the refund. The 'arrived' tap and the chat messages show only that the driver set his marker and stated his position ('I am at the private-hire bay', 21:10:40; 'I am here beside the sign', 21:11:45); a self-set status and a party's own words cannot stand in for the GPS test the clause names.\n\nBecause the sole evidence for the deciding fact — in-geofence arrival and dwell — is the missing trace, impaired under POL-NS-08(b), the case escalates under POL-NS-09(e); the confidence the ruling can carry is capped at that artifact's weight, 0.0, which is below the 0.70 floor (POL-GEN-02(2), POL-NS-09(a)).\n\nOn the remaining arguments:\n- POL-NS-04 does not apply, and both advocates correctly say so. The driver replied at 21:11:45, fifteen seconds after the rider's 21:11:30 message, inside the 120-second window limb (b) allows; its rider-presence limb (c) is undecidable because the rider_track is absent (POL-NS-04), which is neutral, not adverse to the rider.\n- POL-NS-05 (false arrival marker) and POL-NS-06 (waiting-period shortfall) cannot be run — both require a GPS fix matched to the arrival timestamp, and there is none. The 21:10:20-to-21:15:40 span (320 seconds; wait_time_min 5.3) is the driver's own marker, not an in-geofence dwell, and does not establish limb (c). The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09109-01 is also MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-NS-06(i) is unavailable and cannot be asserted to excuse anything.\n- The amount is arithmetically sound: fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee of SGD 6.00 is the GREATER of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_X tier fee (SGD 4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect.\n- On the profiles: the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d is 1 over 120 completed trips, a rate of 0.008), and POL-NS-09(c) and (d) do not fire (0 no-show disputes between this pair); no driver compensation is payable on this record.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: can the driver's GPS export for 21:10:20-21:15:40 (or the rider's track) be produced? That, and only that, will settle POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c)."
  },
