    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: I cannot decide this dispute on the record as it stands, so the SGD 6.00 cancellation fee is placed on hold and the case goes to a human reviewer. It is neither collected nor refunded while that review is pending.\n\nA no-show fee is chargeable only if all four conditions in POL-NS-01 are met. Limbs (a) and (d) are met from the trip record (EV-TRIP-09109): a driver 'arrived' event at 21:10:20, and termination by the driver at 21:15:40 coded RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding. Limbs (b) and (c) are not. Limb (b) needs the GPS trace to put the car inside the pickup geofence at or before 21:10:20, and limb (c) needs the in-geofence dwell — timed from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, not from the arrival tap — to reach 300 seconds for a TRANSPORT_HUB bay. The only artifact that could supply either measurement is EV-GPS-09109, and it is MISSING: no payload, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT (blocking). Under POL-GEN-02(3) a MISSING artifact carries no fact. So limbs (b) and (c) are simply not established.\n\nThat same absence does not hand the rider a refund either. Every refund route reads the trace that is missing. POL-NS-02 refunds in full only where the trace exists and contains no qualifying in-radius fix, and the clause itself treats a deficient trace as impairment rather than as proof the driver was elsewhere. POL-NS-03, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-06 each need their own GPS measurement (stationary within 400 m; distance or speed at the arrival marker; a measured in-geofence dwell), and none can be run. POL-NS-04 is closed on its own terms: the driver answered the rider's 21:11:30 message at 21:11:45, fifteen seconds later and inside the 120-second window limb (b) allows, and its rider-presence limb cannot be run at all because the rider_track is absent — which that clause makes neutral, not adverse. The 21:10:20-to-21:15:40 bracket (320 seconds, wait_time_min 5.3) is measured from the driver's arrival tap; limbs (c) and POL-NS-06 compute dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix, and with no trace that start cannot be fixed, so the bracket cannot stand in for the GPS measurement.\n\nI have weighed the parties' statements. The driver's account that he was at the bay for the full waiting period, and the in-app messages asserting presence, are accounts — not the gps_trace that limbs (b) and (c) read. Where the test admitted no reading at all, an account offered in its place stands in for the test: it does not raise the confidence cap and does not displace the missing trace as the only evidence for the arrival and dwell facts. The messages contain no admission against the driver's interest, and the written statement is not a contemporaneous record. The arrival and dwell questions therefore remain genuinely open.\n\nConfidence is capped by the evidence the ruling rests on. The only candidate evidence for the deciding arrival/dwell fact is EV-GPS-09109 at weight 0.0, below the 0.70 floor, so the case escalates under POL-NS-09(a), and equally because the sole evidence for the deciding fact is unavailable (POL-NS-08 and POL-NS-09(e)). The behaviour-based triggers do not fire — no_show_terminations_30d is 1 (well under 4) and 1/120 = 0.008 (under 0.08), and no repeat-dispute counts — so they are not the reason for escalation.\n\nTwo subsidiary points, neither of which changes the outcome. The SGD 6.00 charged is arithmetically correct: it is the GREATER of the TRANSPORT_HUB zone-class fee (SGD 6.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect. And the missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-09109-01) merely makes the POL-NS-06(i) accumulation route unavailable, which does not matter while there is no trace to accumulate. No clause produces a referral on these facts.\n\nOpen question for the reviewer: can the driver's GPS export for the waiting window be produced, or reconstructed from platform telemetry? If it shows qualifying in-geofence fixes for at least 300 seconds, the fee stands and driver compensation under POL-NS-07 can be considered; if it shows none, the fee is refunded in full under POL-NS-02 / POL-NS-06."
